<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Montgomery, Alabama</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Montgomery is the capital of the US state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alabama">Alabama</a>, on the Alabama River. In February 1861 delegates of seceding states met there to form the Confederate States of America, and it was the Confederate capital until May 1861. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montgomery-bus-boycott">Montgomery bus boycott</a> of 1955–1956, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther-king-jr">Martin Luther King Jr.</a>, was a turning point of the civil rights movement.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/montgomery-alabama.jpg" alt="Montgomery, Alabama" width="320" height="222" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carol M. Highsmith · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_view_of_Montgomery,_Alabama_LCCN2011646683.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
